<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#olive-oil">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olive oil</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olive oil is the oil pressed from olives, a staple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> diet, lighting and trade since antiquity. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> it was among the products of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>'s agrarian economy. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> imported it from the Mediterranean world in exchange for African goods.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olive-oil.jpg" alt="Olive oil" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poyraz 72 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oliven_V1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
